{"tool_name":"relex","contents":["oeb","bioschemas","biotools"],"fetched_metadata":{"biotools":{"id":"relex","home":"http://fields.scripps.edu/relex/","summary":"Calculation of ion current ratios from LC-MS data (requires Xcalibur).","addition_date":"2017-01-17T14:51:41Z","last_update_date":"2019-03-26T08:37:29Z","tool_type":["Desktop application"],"collections":["Proteomics","ms-utils"],"biotools_curie":"biotools:relex","credit":[{"email":"webmaster@ms-utils.org","typeEntity":"Person","typeRole":["Documentor"],"url":"http://ms-utils.org"}],"edit_permission":{"authors":["proteomics.bio.tools"],"type":"group"},"function":[{"input":[{"data":{"term":"Peptide identification","uri":"http://edamontology.org/data_0945"},"format":[{"term":"Thermo RAW","uri":"http://edamontology.org/format_3712"},{"term":"dta","uri":"http://edamontology.org/format_3652"}]}],"operation":[{"term":"18O labeling","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_3640"},{"term":"Filtering","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_3695"},{"term":"Isotope-coded protein label","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_3705"},{"term":"Label-free quantification","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_3634"},{"term":"Labeled quantification","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_3635"},{"term":"Metabolic labeling","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_3715"},{"term":"Peak detection","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_3215"},{"term":"Protein quantification","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_3630"},{"term":"Regression analysis","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_3659"}],"output":[{"data":{"term":"Expression data","uri":"http://edamontology.org/data_2603"},"format":[{"term":"Textual format","uri":"http://edamontology.org/format_2330"}]}]}],"name":"RelEx","owner":"msutils_import","publication":[{"metadata":{"abstract":"Quantitative shotgun proteomic analyses are facilitated using chemical tags such as ICAT and metabolic labeling strategies with stable isotopes. The rapid high-throughput production of quantitative \"shotgun\" proteomic data necessitates the development of software to automatically convert mass spectrometry-derived data of peptides into relative protein abundances. We describe a computer program called RelEx, which uses a least-squares regression for the calculation of the peptide ion current ratios from the mass spectrometry-derived ion chromatograms. RelEx is tolerant of poor signal-to-noise data and can automatically discard nonusable chromatograms and outlier ratios. We apply a simple correction for systematic errors that improves the accuracy of the quantitative measurement by 32 \u00b1 4%. Our automated approach was validated using labeled mixtures composed of known molar ratios and demonstrated in a real sample by measuring the effect of osmotic stress on protein expression in Saccharomyces cerevisiae.","authors":[{"name":"Liu H."},{"name":"MacCoss M.J."},{"name":"Sadygov R."},{"name":"Wu C.C."},{"name":"Yates III J.R."}],"citationCount":237,"date":"2003-12-15T00:00:00Z","journal":"Analytical Chemistry","title":"A Correlation Algorithm for the Automated Quantitative Analysis of Shotgun Proteomics Data"},"pmid":"14670053"}],"topic":[{"term":"Proteomics","uri":"http://edamontology.org/topic_0121"},{"term":"Proteomics experiment","uri":"http://edamontology.org/topic_3520"},{"term":"Statistics and probability","uri":"http://edamontology.org/topic_2269"}],"validated":1},"bioschemas":{"name":"RelEx","home":"https://bio.tools/relex","summary":"Calculation of ion current ratios from LC-MS data (requires Xcalibur).","tool_type":"sc:SoftwareApplication"},"oeb":{"metrics":[{"@id":"https://openebench.bsc.es/monitor/metrics/biotools:relex/app/fields.scripps.edu","@license":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/","@nmsp":"biotools","@type":"metrics","deprecated":true,"distribution":{"sourcecode":{}},"project":{"build":{},"deployment":{},"publications":[{"entries":[{"cit_count":92,"citations":[{"count":1,"year":"2021"},{"count":2,"year":